WEBVTT

00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:15,700
Do genetics tell a person about the best diet?

00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:21,340
No, so genetics don't tell a person about the best diet,

00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:26,340
but genetics do tell us if the person could have issues

00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:30,700
with gluten, could have issues with dairy,

00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:37,820
and some of the other,

00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:42,820
other foods that could be related to those things.

00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:50,180
So if I have a gene defect that's related to the gluten,

00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:56,260
that is the gluten genes,

00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:00,740
I have an increased chance of having gluten sensitivity,

00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:05,180
or I have an increased the other defect for the celiac gene,

00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:08,740
you have an increased risk of having celiac.

00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:11,380
Doesn't mean you're going to remember gene defects,

00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:14,140
doesn't mean you absolutely have that issue.

00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:16,260
It means you have a defect on that,

00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:19,340
and you have a greater chance of having a problem with that,

00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:21,100
doesn't mean you're going to.

00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:23,220
So it gives us, that's why I speak

00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:26,380
throughout the whole genetic course about it gives you clues,

00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:28,300
it gives us clues.

00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,980
So if I have defects on that pathway,

00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:35,540
we make recommendations in our genetic summary,

00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:37,780
in genetic action step sheets,

00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:41,860
that maybe it'd be a good idea to decrease gluten,

00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:46,140
or to decrease dairy based upon your genes.

00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:50,060
It doesn't mean that you have antibodies to gluten,

00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:51,860
or antibodies to dairy.

00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:53,060
In order to find out that,

00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:54,780
you'd have to run an antibody test,

00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:57,340
and we recommend the Cyrex test.

00:01:57,340 --> 00:02:00,900
So the Cyrex test measures antibodies for different foods.

00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:04,860
So remember, genetic picture of somebody

00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,980
doesn't tell us a condition.

00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:10,700
The genetic picture tells us some precursors

00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:13,460
to what could lead to conditions,

00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:17,380
and precursors that could lead to just some issues.

00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:21,220
So it's not going to tell us what's the best perfect diet

00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:26,420
for somebody, it's going to tell us some clues.

